    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Pre-existing eligible services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991#sch-2-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, immediately before the repeal of section 104 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1989:\n\n(a) a person was supplying a value added service, or a private\nnetwork service, within the meaning of that Act:\n\n(i) that was connected to a telecommunications network\noperated by a carrier within the meaning of that Act;\nand\n\n(ii) in respect of the supply of which the person had\nobtained the carrier’s approval; and\n\n(b) because of subsection 104(1) of that Act, the service was\ntaken to be supplied under a class licence within the meaning\nof that Act;\nthen, so far as it is supplied after that repeal, the service is taken to\nbe an eligible service supplied under a class licence within the\nmeaning of the Telecommunications Act 1991.\n\n(2) However, if at any time after that repeal the person supplies the\nservice in a way that is not in accordance with that approval,\nsubsection (1) ceases to apply in relation to the supply of the\nservice by the person.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, immediately before the repeal of section 104 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1989:\n\n(a) a person was supplying a value added service, or a private\nnetwork service, within the meaning of that Act:\n\n(i) that was connected to a telecommunications network\noperated by a carrier within the meaning of that Act;\nand\n\n(ii) in respect of the supply of which the person had\nobtained the carrier’s approval; and\n\n(b) because of subsection 104(1) of that Act, the service was\ntaken to be supplied under a class licence within the meaning\nof that Act;\nthen, so far as it is supplied after that repeal, the service is taken to\nbe an eligible service supplied under a class licence within the\nmeaning of the Telecommunications Act 1991.\n\n(2) However, if at any time after that repeal the person supplies the\nservice in a way that is not in accordance with that approval,\nsubsection (1) ceases to apply in relation to the supply of the\nservice by the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-12-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e94e9090afc2b0d0eba2398da5a329855738d54f0079439b836cb7421ab03264"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991#sch-2-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Pre-existing eligible services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, immediately before the repeal of section 104 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1989:\n\n(a) a person was supplying a value added service, or a private\nnetwork service, within the meaning of that Act:\n\n(i) that was connected to a telecommunications network\noperated by a carrier within the meaning of that Act;\nand\n\n(ii) in respect of the supply of which the person had\nobtained the carrier’s approval; and\n\n(b) because of subsection 104(1) of that Act, the service was\ntaken to be supplied under a class licence within the meaning\nof that Act;\nthen, so far as it is supplied after that repeal, the service is taken to\nbe an eligible service supplied under a class licence within the\nmeaning of the Telecommunications Act 1991.\n\n(2) However, if at any time after that repeal the person supplies the\nservice in a way that is not in accordance with that approval,\nsubsection (1) ceases to apply in relation to the supply of the\nservice by the person."
    },
